I found one setup need and no missing dependencies. On JDK 25, XJC 2.1.13 crashes before it generates any code unless JAXB's optimized-accessor code generation is turned off. Setting `com.sun.xml.bind.v2.bytecode.ClassTailor.noOptimize=true` fixes it: with the property set, it compiled a test schema into `ObjectFactory.java`, `Person.java` and `package-info.java`. The existing CXF 2.6.1 JAXB test in this repo sets the same property for the same reason.

The library's published dependencies already pull in everything else it needs (JAXB runtime and API 2.1, StAX API, activation), so the dependency list stays empty. It doesn't need Docker either: XJC is an offline XSD-to-Java code generator.

